# SecuBox Profiles — the /profiles/ panel (User=secubox) delegates apply/rollback
# to the root helper secubox-profilectl (webui→ctl pattern, see
# .claude/MODULE-COMPLIANCE.md → Privileged Operations).
#
# The CLI is launched via `systemd-run`, NOT plain sudo: this service runs under
# ProtectSystem=strict with a reduced ReadWritePaths, and a `sudo` child inherits
# that mount namespace — the CLI would see the snapshot dir, audit log, WAF routes
# and /data/lxc as READ-ONLY (EROFS) and could not drive systemd/LXC. A transient
# `systemd-run` unit runs in PID 1's context, OUTSIDE the sandbox, with the access
# the actuator needs.
#
# Exact-command grants (no wildcards, no flag escapes) — the panel always builds
# this FIXED argv (--only stays a root-CLI-only affordance):
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-profilectl apply --yes --json
secubox ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --wait --pipe --collect --quiet /usr/sbin/secubox-profilectl rollback --yes --json
